    "body": "## Motivation\n\nSince #44993, `TopK` folds `routed_scaling_factor` into the top-k weights whenever the layer's quant method reports `fuse_routed_scaling_factor_in_topk`. `KTEPWrapperMethod` forwards unknown attributes to its GPU method through `__getattr__`, and the MXFP4 methods (`mxfp4_flashinfer_cutlass_moe`, `mxfp4_marlin_moe`, `mxfp4_flashinfer_trtllm_moe`) report `True`. So under KTransformers the top-k weights already carry the factor.\n\n`DeepseekV2MoE.forward_normal` and `forward_normal_dual_stream` still multiply the routed output by `routed_scaling_factor` unconditionally whenever the quant method is `KTEPWrapperMethod`. The routed experts were therefore scaled twice. On DeepSeek-V4.1 (`routed_scaling_factor` 1.5) they came out at 2.25x instead of 1.5x, on every layer.\n\n## Modifications\n\nThe KT branch of that condition now scales only when the top-k has not already folded the factor (`not self.routed_scaling_factor_fused_in_topk`). Both sites are changed. GPU methods that do not fuse the factor keep the single multiply they had before.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (1017 checkpoint), KTransformers hybrid MoE on 2x RTX 5070 Ti (TP2) with AVX2 MXFP4 CPU experts.\n\n- **Reference.** Teacher-forced log-probs on 24 x 480-token pieces (11,496 scored tokens) from the checkpoint's own `inference/model.py`, streamed one layer at a time.\n- **Layer 0.** I dumped piece 0's MoE pieces on both sides from the same input.\n  - The routing and the top-k weights are identical, and the weights already sum to 1.5 per token.\n  - The shared expert matches within 0.2%.\n  - The KT routed output is 1.50x the reference.\n  - With one scale, the residual stream after layer 0 matches the reference within 1.9%; before this fix it was 13%.\n\n| | mean NLL | vs reference (paired, per token) |\n|---|---|---|\n| reference (`inference/model.py`) | 2.5940 | |\n| before | 2.8780 | +0.2839 (SE 0.0116) |\n| after | 2.5960 | +0.0020 (SE 0.0046) |\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThe speed is unchanged:\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| decode (tok/s) | 45.6 | 45.6 |\n| 35K-token prefill (tok/s) | 1,432 | 1,420 |\n\nBoth rows are the second run on the same setup.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01C2UBZdnrDZSBh8yQz8rc9g\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39773386704](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39773386704)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39773386452](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39773386452)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39773386369](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39773386369)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
